PATCH 322: promote + reconstruct the missing 22dd render-script handler 0x41df (-> dc12 object/vehicle
geometry-record poster) so FUN_0000_22dd RETURNS and the 459a mission loop ITERATES (c452 advances).

THE ACTUAL ROOT CAUSE (asm + gdb verified; the predecessor's "spin in the op-0x4c present pump inside the
extender gate" premise was a MISDIAGNOSIS).  The mission ACCEPT path reaches FUN_0000_459a (the fixed-
timestep mission game loop).  Its OUTER do-loop already pumps the cooperative INT-8 tick every frame
(patch 295: `fist_timer_pump()` at the top), then renders via FUN_0000_22dd().  BUT 22dd NEVER RETURNS:

  22dd (asm 0x22dd, DS=DGROUP): render branch does `c450=3; do { call word[DGROUP:word[0x4a86]] }
  while(c450!=0)` -- a threaded-code interpreter walking a per-phase script table (cursor DAT_2000_0a86,
  each handler advances the cursor +2; the phase terminator 23ce clears c450 -> loop exits).

gdb on the live spin (BATTLES(160,100)->OK(205,128)->ACCEPT(40,186), FIST_TICK_HZ=25000): the do-while
calls fist_icall_near(0, 0x41df) forever, cursor frozen, c452==1.  The phase-0x20 script from the cursor is
[41df, 378e, 23ce] -- 378e/23ce are registered, but 0x41df is a script MID-ENTRY Ghidra never promoted, so
fist_icall(0x41df) misses the fmap (g_mem[0x41de]==0xc3, not a leading nop) and returns the no-op
trap_tramp -> the cursor never advances -> the interpreter spins -> 22dd never returns -> 459a's outer
loop (and its patch-295 pump) never re-runs -> c452 frozen at 1 -> the per-tick flight model (c0ca/461b) +
terrain-follow never run.  EXACT same class as patch 193 (0x41d0) and patch 306 (0x41c7).

0x41df (asm, verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin): `call dc12; movw 0,[0x4b9e]; addw 2,[0x4a86]; ret`
-- identical shape to 0x41d0, calling dc12 instead of db99.

FUN_0000_dc12 (asm 0xdc12-0xdd14) -- the OBJECT/VEHICLE geometry-record poster, sibling of db99:
  - call ddff (the shared record prolog); es:di = word[0xea2e]:word[0xea2c] = the extender-TCB record base
    (patch-068 DAT_2000_aa2c macro).
  - copy the camera fields d548-struct [0x12..0x1c] -> rec[0x2c..0x36]; rec[0x38]=word[0x1558]; rec[0x58]=5.
  - si = word[0x6d34] = the player-vehicle node NEAR OFFSET (DAT_2000_2d34).  Object-delta select:
      * node[0x1c]!=0 (object): bx=word[DGROUP:node[0x1b]*8+0x6d3c]; if bx!=0 -> ax=b112(obj,veh),
        rec[0x56]=ax, rec[0x58]|=2.
      * else (non-object): bx=word[DGROUP:node[0x1b]*2+0x7d2a]; if byte[DGROUP:bx]!=0 ->
        ax=0731(bx+0xc, veh+4)+0x80@ah, rec[0x56]=ax, rec[0x58]|=2.
      * both tables empty (dc9a): if node[0x19]&0x80 -> rec[0x58]=(|2)&0xfb; rec[0x56]=word[veh+0x8e];
        rec[0x58]|=2.  (bit7 clear -> je dcb7: rec[0x56]/rec[0x58] untouched.)
  - rec[0x3e]=byte[0x154a]<<6 (ah=[0x154a];al=0;shr ax,2); rec[0x2]=word[DGROUP:word[0x156a]] (page seg);
    rec[0x4]=0; inbox rec[0x3f2]=EBX; op word[0xea10] = (word[0xea12]!=0 ? 0x10 : 0x5c); call e339.

BASE-LOSS: the vehicle/object near offsets index DGROUP -> rebased g_mem+0x1c000+off; b112/0731 (the
already-reconstructed object-delta helpers) take those as host pointers (param_1<->si, param_2<->di,
matched vs the af1c b112 call site: b112(other,self) => here b112(object,vehnode)).  EBX inbox is PROVABLY
DEAD for these display-list ops (the PM op-handler reloads ebx=[0xc93] before use, per patch 193's op-0xc
analysis) -> written 0, not fabricated.  Live-verified on AZER1: node[0x1c]==0 && node[0x19]&0x80 -> the
word[veh+0x8e] path (b112/0731 skipped this frame; both branches reconstructed for faithfulness).

RESULT (default `make native`, mission ACCEPT path): 22dd returns, the 459a outer loop iterates, c452
advances one tick per frame (patch 295's pump), op 0x24 re-posts every frame, and the mission FB changes
frame-to-frame (the flight-model sim + radar now advance).  MISSION-PATH ONLY (the 22dd render script is
reached only inside the d548-gated in-mission 459a loop) -> strictly behaviour-neutral for the 24 menu/
pre-mission verify flows (d548==0 in the menu; 41df/dc12 have no menu callers).  Sources stay pristine
(re_out/fist.c 61453e42); patched via build/.

